I wonder if this has been asked before, since I could not find any
discussion about this after searching this group.  I guess maybe there
are just too few nethackers who speak Chinese.

In Chinese mythology, Huan Ti (or should be correctly spelled as "Huang
Ti", the Yellow Emperor) is credited with ending ancient chaos,
founding the "Middle Kingdom" and inventing many things that Chinese
use.  He is also worshiped by Taoists as the founder of their religion.
 I believe he should be the lawful god if we consider his role in
Chinese mythology, or the neutral god if we take him as the founder of
Taoism, which preaches "leave things as they are".

Maybe the definitions of "lawful", "neutral", and "chaotic" in AD&D
suggest otherwise so that the Devteam is right about this setting.
However, it just looks queer to people who speak Chinese.



